/-!
# The covering sieves of a big fppf site are generated pretopology-style

The Grothendieck topology of a big fppf site is defined as the topology *generated* by the
site's chosen fppf covering families, through `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.Saturate`, so a
covering sieve carries no chosen family with it: it is only built from them by the pullback
and local-character axioms. This file shows that nothing is lost — a sieve is covering exactly
when it *contains* a chosen covering family — and draws the consequence for descent along
covering sieves.

This is the first step of Stacks 02W8, in the shape in which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve` consumes it. The source
performs that step by invoking Descent, Lemma 02W3, whose proof begins by refining the given
fppf covering by a chosen one; in the covering-sieve shape the rest of 02W3 — comparing the
categories of descent data along the refinement — is *free*, because the datum of a descent
problem along a sieve `T` is a family indexed by the arrows of `T`, which simply restricts to
a smaller sieve, and the object whose representability is at stake, the fibre product
`X ×[Y] yoneda.obj a`, does not mention `T` at all. So the whole of step 1 which the
covering-sieve predicate needs is the refinement, and that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_isCovering` below.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.mem_topology_iff`: a sieve is covering for the topology of a
  big fppf site if and only if it contains a chosen covering family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology`: the family form of the
  previous statement, in the big fppf site and in its slice over `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.jointlySurjective_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isCovering`:
  the geometric content of a chosen covering family — joint surjectivity, flatness and local
  finite presentation of its members.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_isCovering`: **step 1 of
  Stacks 02W8 for the covering sieves.** To prove effective descent along every covering sieve
  it suffices to prove it along the sieves generated by the chosen covering families.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_zariskiCover_of_isCovering`:
  step 1 composed with the glueing step, which is what the remaining steps of Stacks 02W8 are
  to be proved against — only the Zariski covering of the descended sheaf is left, and it is
  asked for a chosen fppf covering family rather than for a saturated covering sieve.

## Implementation notes

**No cardinal hypothesis is incurred.** The chosen family extracted from a covering sieve is
indexed by a type in `Type (u + 1)` and is used only as a family: no coproduct of its members
is formed inside the site, so the site's cutoff is never consulted. A coproduct would not be
available — the cutoff is only a strong prelimit, with no bound on its cofinality — which is
why step 1 stops at a *family* and not at the single surjective flat morphism of finite
presentation of affines that Descent, Lemma 02W3 reduces to in the source.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02W8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02W3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02W3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 021R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 021U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021U)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace BigFppfSite

/-- **A sieve of a big fppf site is covering exactly when it contains a chosen covering
family.** This is the pretopology-style description of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.topology`, which is defined as the topology *generated* by the
chosen families; it holds because those families contain the isomorphisms and are stable under
base change and refinement. -/
@[sga "3 IV 4.2.6" "partial", sga "4 II 1.4" "special case"]
theorem mem_topology_iff (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {X : B.Schemes} {T : Sieve X} :
    T ∈ B.topology X ↔ ∃ R ∈ B.precoverage X, R ≤ T.arrows :=
  Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition

/-- **Every covering sieve of a big fppf site contains a chosen covering family**, in family
form: the arrows of the family, not merely the presieve it generates, are arrows of the
sieve. -/
theorem exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {X : B.Schemes} {T : Sieve X}
    (hT : T ∈ B.topology X) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X, B.IsCovering ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ ∀ i, T (E.f i) := by
  obtain ⟨R, hR, hRT⟩ := B.mem_topology_iff.1 hT
  obtain ⟨E, hEq, hE⟩ := hR
  exact ⟨E, hE, fun i ↦ hRT _ _ (show R (E.f i) from hEq ▸ E.presieve₀_f i)⟩

/-- The geometric content of a chosen covering family of a big fppf site: its members are
jointly surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation. -/
theorem jointlySurjective_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isCovering
    (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {X : B.Schemes} {E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X}
    (hE : B.IsCovering ⟨X, E⟩) :
    (∀ x : B.inclusion.obj X, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range (B.inclusion.map (E.f i)).base) ∧
      ∀ i, Flat (B.inclusion.map (E.f i)) ∧
        LocallyOfFinitePresentation (B.inclusion.map (E.f i)) := by
  have h := B.isFppfCovering_of_isCovering hE
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IsFppfCovering, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff,
    ← PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map, Scheme.fppfPrecoverage,
    PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀, Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff] at h
  exact h

end BigFppfSite

namespace BigFppfOver

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology` in the big fppf category
over `S`: every covering sieve of an object of the slice contains a covering family of the
slice.

A sieve of the slice is covering exactly when the corresponding sieve of the underlying object
is, by `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff`, and a chosen covering family of the
underlying object is lifted to the slice by equipping each of its sources with the composite
structure morphism, which leaves the underlying family unchanged. -/
theorem exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : B.Contains S) {a : BigFppfOver B S hS} {T : Sieve a}
    (hT : T ∈ BigFppfOver.topology B S hS a) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} a,
      BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS ⟨a, E⟩ ∧ ∀ i, T (E.f i) := by
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff] at hT
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hET⟩ := B.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology hT
  exact ⟨⟨E.I₀, fun i ↦ Over.mk (E.f i ≫ a.hom), fun i ↦ Over.homMk (E.f i)⟩, hE,
    fun i ↦ (Sieve.overEquiv_iff T (E.f i)).1 (hET i)⟩

end BigFppfOver

namespace Space

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- **Step 1 of Stacks 02W8 for the covering sieves: effective descent along a covering sieve
need only be proved along the sieves generated by the site's chosen covering families.**

Descent, Lemma 02W3 opens the proof of Stacks 02W8 by replacing an arbitrary fppf covering by
a single surjective flat morphism of finite presentation of affines. Its first move, and the
only one the covering-sieve predicate needs, is the refinement of the given covering: here, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology`, every covering sieve
contains a chosen covering family. The comparison of descent data along the refinement, which
is the rest of 02W3, costs nothing in this shape — the hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve` is a condition on the arrows of
the sieve, so it restricts to the smaller sieve for free, and its conclusion is a statement
about `pullback f h`, which does not mention the sieve.

It stops at a *family*: the further reduction to one morphism would need the coproduct of the
family inside the site, and the site's cutoff is only a strong prelimit, with no bound on its
cofinality. -/
theorem isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_isCovering {P : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}}
    (H : ∀ ⦃X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u⦄ (f : X ⟶ Y),
      Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) X →
      Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) Y →
      ∀ ⦃a : BigFppfOver B S hS⦄ (h : yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y)
        (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} a), BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS ⟨a, E⟩ →
        (∀ i, (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
          (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map (E.f i) ≫ h))) →
        (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf (pullback.snd f h)) :
    IsEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve B S hS P := by
  intro X Y f hX hY a h T hTmem hall
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hET⟩ := BigFppfOver.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology B S hS hTmem
  exact H f hX hY h E hE fun i ↦ hall (E.f i) (hET i)

/-- **What is left of Stacks 02W8 for the covering sieves after step 1 and step 5.** Effective
descent along the covering sieves at a property which is Zariski local on the target and
satisfies fppf descent follows from producing, for a descent datum along a *chosen fppf
covering family*, a Zariski covering of the descended sheaf by representable open subfunctors
indexed by a type smaller than the cofinality of the site's cutoff.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_zariskiCover` — the
glueing step, Tag 0AP4 — with its covering sieve replaced by a chosen covering family, by step
1. It is the form in which the remaining steps of Stacks 02W8 are to be proved: the family
hands over joint surjectivity and the flatness and local finite presentation of its members,
by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.jointlySurjective_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isCovering`,
where a saturated covering sieve hands over nothing.

The three remaining steps of Stacks 02W8 are exactly the construction of that covering:
enlarge an affine open of the descended object to a quasi-compact open stable under the
descent datum, using universal openness of flat morphisms of finite presentation (Stacks
01UA); observe that such an open is quasi-affine over the base (Stacks 02LR); and descend it
(Stacks 0247). -/
theorem isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_zariskiCover_of_isCovering
    {P : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}} [IsZariskiLocalAtTarget P]
    [P.DescendsAlong (@Surjective ⊓ @Flat ⊓ @LocallyOfFinitePresentation)]
    (H : ∀ ⦃X Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u⦄ (f : X ⟶ Y),
      Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) X →
      Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) Y →
      ∀ ⦃a : BigFppfOver B S hS⦄ (h : yoneda.obj a ⟶ Y)
        (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} a), BigFppfOver.IsCovering B S hS ⟨a, E⟩ →
        (∀ i, (P.inverseImage (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).presheaf
          (pullback.snd f (yoneda.map (E.f i) ≫ h))) →
        ∃ (ι : Type u) (_ : Nonempty ι), Cardinal.mk ι < B.cutoff.ord.cof ∧
          ∃ (W : ι → BigFppfOver B S hS) (k : ∀ i, yoneda.obj (W i) ⟶ pullback f h),
            (∀ i, IsOpenImmersion B S hS (k i)) ∧
              Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (Sigma.desc k)) :
    IsEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve B S hS P := by
  refine isEffectiveDescentAlongCoveringSieve_of_zariskiCover ?_
  intro X Y f hX hY a h T hTmem hall
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hET⟩ := BigFppfOver.exists_isCovering_of_mem_topology B S hS hTmem
  exact H f hX hY h E hE fun i ↦ hall (E.f i) (hET i)

end Space

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
